00:06:28.735 --> 00:06:34.035
Survivorship bias, and this is how it works, scores a fund, a strategy, or a forecaster

00:06:34.035 --> 00:06:36.035
only on the record still in the sample.

00:06:36.695 --> 00:06:42.095
Shut funds, delisted stocks, and deleted accounts fall out, and the average of whoever remains

00:06:42.095 --> 00:06:44.735
looks kinder than the average of everyone who tried.

00:06:45.255 --> 00:06:49.915
A 2026 study of India's nifty small cap, 250 walks the arithmetic.

00:06:49.915 --> 00:06:55.215
The author rebuilt membership with a market cap ranking from price and volume, including

00:06:55.215 --> 00:07:03.395
delisted names in the exchanges Bav copy files across 1,437 stocks and 9 years, 2016 through

00:07:03.395 --> 00:07:04.215
2025.

00:07:04.915 --> 00:07:09.315
An equal weight book of only today's members was set next to an equal weight book of everyone

00:07:09.315 --> 00:07:15.655
who had ever been in, keeping only the survivors overstated annual returns by 4.94 percentage

00:07:15.655 --> 00:07:16.055
points.

00:07:16.055 --> 00:07:26.095
a 23.3% overstatement and overstated sharp ratios by 0.097, a 9.1% overstatement. Turnover

00:07:26.095 --> 00:07:34.315
in that window was 82.5%, 16.1% of the names were delisted, 33.1% graduated out of

00:07:34.315 --> 00:07:40.835
the small cap index, and 33.2% were demoted. All three groups fed the bias, so it is not

00:07:40.835 --> 00:07:47.395
only bankruptcies. The rebuilt list matched current members perfectly and was estimated at 85-90%

00:07:47.395 --> 00:07:53.535
accurate on older membership. That missing slice is the method's own ceiling. A 2010 review of

00:07:53.535 --> 00:07:58.675
finance paper is described as the first to calculate, test and explain different definitions of

00:07:58.675 --> 00:08:04.855
this bias in mutual fund performance instead of one headline gap. The link between survival and performance

00:08:04.855 --> 00:08:09.875
was stronger for small funds. Funds that did not survive significantly underperformed.

00:08:10.375 --> 00:08:15.415
New funds did not significantly outperform, which argues against reading the gap as brilliant

00:08:15.415 --> 00:08:21.015
newcomers simply replacing an old book. The paper's practical warning is that cleaning one famous

00:08:21.015 --> 00:08:26.695
database does not end the problem. It remains wherever survivor-free data is missing, and some

00:08:26.695 --> 00:08:32.115
methods still need a truncated sample. Two analysts can quote two different penalties from the same

00:08:32.115 --> 00:08:34.595
graveyard because the definition changes the number.

00:08:35.135 --> 00:08:40.635
A screenshot of forecast still online or a strategy page that shows only accounts still trading

00:08:40.965 --> 00:08:43.095
is that current constituent portfolio.

00:08:43.655 --> 00:08:49.295
The 4.94 point gap showed up because the levers were put back in, not because the survivors

00:08:49.295 --> 00:08:50.455
returns were invented.

00:08:51.015 --> 00:08:54.895
Until the disappeared names are counted, the average describes who stayed.

00:08:55.355 --> 00:08:56.835
It does not describe the method.

